# Magic and Military — project context

Public site to **publish and read** the manga **Magic and Military** chapter by chapter. The home page is the chapter index; `/<chapter-slug>` hosts the reader.

## Stack in this repo

| Layer | Choice |
|---|---|
| Framework | Next.js 16 (App Router) |
| UI | React 19, Tailwind CSS v4 |
| Content | Chapter pages are private UploadThing files; chapter data in `app/_constants/chapters.ts` (public) and `lib/chapterManifest.ts` (server-only keys) |
| Tooling | Biome, ESLint, Husky, commitlint, lint-staged, `tsc-baseline` |
| Package manager | pnpm |

## Information architecture

| Route | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `/` | Home: animated title hero, ordered chapter links, social footer |
| `/<chapter-slug>` | Chapter reader: static shell, `ProtectedReader` client leaf, only published chapters (`publishedAt`) |
| `/api/pages/<id>` | Same-origin image proxy for private pages (disallowed in `robots.ts`) |

**Reader protection:** file keys never leave `lib/chapterManifest.ts` and must never be exported through a barrel (client components import `@constants`). Pages use a plain `<img>` against the proxy on purpose. Threat model, limits and the add-pages workflow: [docs/audits/reader-protection.md](../../docs/audits/reader-protection.md).

**No global header** on the marketing/home shell. **Footer** is not a colored bar: a single row of social icons (X, Instagram, TikTok). URLs live in [`app/_constants/site.ts`](../../app/_constants/site.ts).

## Home page UX (keep unless product changes)

- **Canvas:** off-white (`--canvas` / `bg-canvas` in [`app/globals.css`](../../app/globals.css)), not pure white.
- **Hero:** centered [`TitleHero`](../../app/_components/TitleHero.tsx) — title **Magic and Military**, **each letter a distinct color**, **subtle staggered fade/slide-in** on load (`prefers-reduced-motion` disables motion).
- **Chapters:** [`ChapterList`](../../app/_components/ChapterList.tsx) — **ordered list** of links; **classic web link** styling (`.link-classic`: blue, underlined, underline removed on hover/focus).
- **Mobile-first:** responsive type scale, padding, and **44px-style** social hit targets in [`SiteFooter`](../../app/_components/SiteFooter.tsx).

## Layout conventions

- **Path aliases:** `@components`, `@constants`, `@utils`, `@/*` (see [`tsconfig.json`](../../tsconfig.json)).
- Non-route folders under `app/` use **`_` prefix** (see **`code-hygiene`**).
- Site-wide copy, chapter placeholders, and social URLs → **`app/_constants/site.ts`** (barrel `@constants`).

## When building features

- Meet **WCAG 2.2 Level AA** (see **`accessibility`**). Hero uses visible letter colors plus `sr-only` full title; chapter list has a screen-reader heading.
- Follow **`server-client-boundaries`** — hero animation is a **client leaf** (`TitleHero`); page stays a Server Component.
- Follow **`code-hygiene`** and **`repo-tooling`** for structure, imports, and git hygiene.
## Sitemap and robots

- [`app/sitemap.ts`](../../app/sitemap.ts) lists every public URL; [`app/robots.ts`](../../app/robots.ts) points crawlers at `/sitemap.xml`. Origin lives in `SITE_URL` (`app/_constants/site.ts`).
- **Whenever you add, rename, or remove a page or route** (including chapters), check `app/sitemap.ts` and update it if the URL is missing or stale. Chapter routes derive from the chapter list in `site.ts`; any other static route needs an explicit entry. Exclude private routes (e.g. admin) and disallow them in `robots.ts`.
